House Price Prediction App 

Hey! This is my project for the Week 5 lab. It's a machine learning web app built with Python and Streamlit. It uses a Random Forest Regression model to predict the median value of a house based on the Boston Housing dataset.

Files in this Project

BostonHousingData.csv: The dataset used to train the model.

train_model.py: The script that pre-processes the data and trains the machine learning model.

app.py: The main Streamlit web application.

requirements.txt: The list of Python libraries needed to run the app.

Quick Setup

Before running anything, make sure you have the required libraries installed. Open your terminal in this folder and run:

pip install pandas scikit-learn joblib streamlit


(Or just run pip install -r requirements.txt if you are using the text file!)

How to Run the Project

This project has two steps: first you train the model, and then you run the web app.

Step 1: Train the model
Run the training script in your terminal. This will clean the dataset, train the Random Forest model, and save it as a house_price_model.pkl file so the app can use it.

python train_model.py


Step 2: Start the Streamlit App
Once the .pkl file is generated, you can start the Streamlit web interface by running:

streamlit run app.py